==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|trēow}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*treu}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*trewą}}. Germanic cognates include {{cog|ofs|trē}}, {{cog|osx|trio}}, {{cog|non|tré}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐍂𐌹𐌿}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ang|trēo|trīo|trīow|trȳw|trēu|trēw}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|n|head=trēow}}

# {{topic|ang|Trees}}[[tree]]
# {{topic|ang|Woods}}[[wood]]
# {{topic|ang|Forests}}(collective) trees, a [[forest]]
# a piece of [[wood]]: [[beam]], [[log]], [[stake]], [[staff]], [[cudgel]]
# [[gallows]]; [[cross]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|tree}} {{l|ang|bēam}}
* {{sense|gallows}} {{l|ang|ġealga}}, {{l|ang|rōd}}

